Embedding exception
-------------------

The OFL's "embedding exception" is what permits these files to be converted into, and shipped as,
binary payloads inside a software distribution. Nothing here is sold on its own, and the fonts are
not the product.

Why the data lives here
-----------------------

The library that consumes it (`rust_widgets`) is capped at 10 MiB per package by crates.io, and
these payloads are already-compressed binaries that gzip cannot shrink. Keeping them in a package
of their own is what lets the library keep growing. Nothing about the licence changes with the
move: the same bytes, the same subsets, the same upstream revisions.
